BEGINTEXT

 Orion's Belt

 A synthetic, hand-authored 3-empire test fixture, not real DOS content. Three
 collinear empires along row 11 of a 21x21 galaxy: the Empire Under Test (EUT,
 slot 0) at x=2, a Near opponent (slot 1) at x=9, and a Far opponent (slot 2)
 at x=21. Chebyshev distance EUT-to-Near is 7; EUT-to-Far is 19 -- an
 unambiguous, ~2.7x near/far margin, built to test whether empire-level
 proximity awareness (CenterOfGravityGene) or target-focus (FocusGene) show
 any real effect once "closer" is well-defined, unlike a symmetric or
 many-opponent layout. No independent worlds are placed at all -- every world
 belongs to one of the three empires from the start, so growth can only come
 from conquering a rival, not from the "expand into empty space" pattern that
 dominates growth in every other scenario used this session.

 All three empires start with identical tech (Bio), identical modifiers
 (CENTRAL), and three worlds each (a capital plus two others) using matched
 population/efficiency/ship/defense loadouts, so the only asymmetry in this
 galaxy is geometry.
ENDTEXT

; No BEGINDESCRIPTION / WorldBackgroundIndex -- purely optional flavor-text
